WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:01:25.400
(Support Admin Watch on kissFlix.co)

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.529
50 million?

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.120
I'm exhausted, sir.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.798
I want to retire.

00:01:40.798 --> 00:01:42.560
I don't want to get in anyone's way anymore.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.610
I think the price I'm asking is fair.

00:01:46.175 --> 00:01:47.520
How dare you!

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.045
Grab him!

00:01:49.045 --> 00:01:51.740
What's this? Let me go!

00:01:57.094 --> 00:02:00.675
You've got the balls to come to my house
and disrespect me?

00:02:00.675 --> 00:02:02.830
You think you're so brave?

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.171
You've got some fucking nerve!

00:02:05.171 --> 00:02:07.459
You piece of shit! How dare you!

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.260
Get him up.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.341
Hey!

00:02:17.227 --> 00:02:19.904
You want a piece of me? You little shit!

00:02:19.904 --> 00:02:22.043
That's enough.

00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:23.844
You don't want to kill him.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.060
Sir?

00:02:34.216 --> 00:02:35.692
He's dead.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.641
Get him out of here.
Weechana has already cleared the way.

00:02:51.862 --> 00:02:55.680
She told me that Weechana threatened you.

00:02:56.806 --> 00:02:58.114
Yeah.

00:02:59.238 --> 00:03:00.942
How'd you get mixed up in all this?

00:03:03.563 --> 00:03:05.142
Pun, come on.

00:03:05.142 --> 00:03:06.923
Please, just tell us.

00:03:06.923 --> 00:03:12.053
Eva and I have our own concerns
about Weechana too.

00:03:12.053 --> 00:03:15.623
If there's anything we should know,
please tell us.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.582
Okay.

00:03:21.723 --> 00:03:25.040
I once saw Weechana
with an actress named Ginny...

00:03:25.731 --> 00:03:26.980
in New York.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.846
They went behind a restaurant
and got into a loud argument.

00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:33.920
I don't think he ever expected
another Thai person to be around,

00:03:34.998 --> 00:03:36.621
but I just happened to be there.

00:03:39.526 --> 00:03:41.680
What were they arguing about?

00:03:43.939 --> 00:03:46.488
It seemed like...

00:03:46.488 --> 00:03:48.640
she wanted to go public
with their relationship.

00:03:52.136 --> 00:03:55.580
So you've known about Weechana
for a long time, haven't you?

00:03:56.747 --> 00:03:59.792
They started arguing
right where I couldn't exactly leave,

00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:01.844
and I ended up seeing Weechana.

00:04:02.795 --> 00:04:05.323
Honestly, I'd completely forgotten about it.

00:04:05.323 --> 00:04:08.520
It was just a coincidence that you and he...

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.888
I still don't get
why Weechana felt the need to threaten you.

00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:20.040
He probably thought I'd told you.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.533
I don't know.

00:04:23.075 --> 00:04:26.712
He also said
he was going to see my uncle in Chinatown,

00:04:27.806 --> 00:04:31.607
which meant he'd already found out who I was.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.358
Okay.

00:04:37.358 --> 00:04:39.139
Your turn.

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:41.320
Tell me what's going on.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.884
Come on.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.384
I should know.

00:04:49.904 --> 00:04:52.200
Can I talk to him for a minute?

00:04:53.718 --> 00:04:55.196
Okay.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.651
Did Pun do something to upset her?

00:05:04.651 --> 00:05:06.400
No, no, no! He's fine.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.382
They just need a moment to talk.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.488
How long have you two been friends?

00:05:16.323 --> 00:05:17.966
Since junior high, I think.

00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:21.155
Back then, we were both tiny,

00:05:21.155 --> 00:05:22.779
so we got picked on all the time.

00:05:22.779 --> 00:05:28.352
We pretty much became friends
from running away from bullies together.

00:05:28.352 --> 00:05:30.512
What about you two?

00:05:30.512 --> 00:05:32.980
Have you known each other for a long time?

00:05:34.706 --> 00:05:38.872
I first met Eva at an awards ceremony.

00:05:38.872 --> 00:05:41.691
Back then, she was a nobody,

00:05:41.691 --> 00:05:44.960
and I was just one of the event coordinators.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:48.400
I saw Eva sitting there,
trying to do her own makeup,

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.931
because none of the makeup artists
would help her.

00:05:49.931 --> 00:05:53.310
So I went out of my way
to find someone who would.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:57.886
Honestly, we became close
because we were both being picked on.

00:05:57.886 --> 00:05:59.000
We were looked down on so much

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.400
that we promised ourselves...

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.240
one day no one would ever treat us
like that again.

00:06:05.956 --> 00:06:08.518
That sounds just like me and Pun.

00:06:08.518 --> 00:06:11.782
Before he left to study abroad,
we promised each other...

00:06:11.782 --> 00:06:14.779
and we stood like this...

00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:16.646
that we'd never let anyone beat us up again.

00:06:16.646 --> 00:06:18.447
We'd do this.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.320
[Weechana's Assistant]

00:06:29.502 --> 00:06:33.000
I found out
that Weechana was cheating on me with Ginny.

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:37.240
That was before we went out for our run.

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:40.281
I see.

00:06:41.043 --> 00:06:43.000
I saw you cried.

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:49.563
You saw that?

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.680
I turned the music up loud,

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.869
but I could still hear it.

00:07:15.182 --> 00:07:17.680
I was going to break up with Weechai.

00:07:19.504 --> 00:07:22.139
But that video...

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:24.976
of you and me out on our run came out first.

00:07:27.243 --> 00:07:28.666
I see.

00:07:30.184 --> 00:07:32.360
When I broke up with him,

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.200
he got me a car.

00:07:38.355 --> 00:07:42.846
Then he pressured me into using it
and posting it on social media.

00:07:42.846 --> 00:07:44.915
Seriously?

00:07:44.915 --> 00:07:47.720
Did he force you
to post that picture on Instagram?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.880
He even sent me a caption to post.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.080
I have to keep dating him

00:08:00.406 --> 00:08:02.360
and help him with his campaign.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.681
He threatened me.

00:08:09.618 --> 00:08:11.419
He threatened my aunt.

00:08:13.222 --> 00:08:15.520
And now he's threatening Domino.

00:08:17.638 --> 00:08:19.896
The day his grandma sent someone
to bring me to the house,

00:08:19.896 --> 00:08:23.646
I realized just how terrifying
this family really is.

00:08:26.654 --> 00:08:29.980
I don't know. Maybe Ginny's death...

00:08:32.176 --> 00:08:33.977
I don't know.

00:08:36.176 --> 00:08:37.595
I'm worried about everything.

00:08:37.595 --> 00:08:40.379
I'm worried
about my aunt, Domino, and my career.

00:08:40.379 --> 00:08:42.338
I don't want any of this to affect my film.

00:08:42.338 --> 00:08:43.960
I really want this role,

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.152
but I just don't have the time
to prepare for it.

00:08:47.152 --> 00:08:50.075
I'm terrified I won't be good enough.

00:08:50.075 --> 00:08:52.640
I'm terrified I'll let everyone down.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.563
I'm terrified I'll disappoint all the fans
who've been waiting for me.

00:08:55.563 --> 00:08:58.320
- I'm scared everything's going to go wrong.
- Eva.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.119
I... I don't know what to do anymore.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.680
I really don't know what...

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.560
what... what I'm supposed to do.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.361
Breathe.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.831
Breathe.

00:09:13.355 --> 00:09:15.280
Do you realize that...

00:09:16.699 --> 00:09:19.310
with everything you've said,

00:09:21.976 --> 00:09:24.110
you haven't mentioned yourself even once?

00:09:28.515 --> 00:09:30.720
What about you?

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.220
Where are you in all of this?

00:09:34.393 --> 00:09:36.689
Why aren't you worried about yourself?

00:09:58.476 --> 00:10:01.289
Oh boy! Look at them.

00:10:46.902 --> 00:10:48.703
I'm sorry...

00:10:49.478 --> 00:10:53.800
that I yelled at you,
and I'm sorry I misjudged you.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.320
- I didn't know...
- It's fine.

00:10:59.495 --> 00:11:01.913
People are so quick...

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.138
to judge others by what they see.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:14.000
They never bother
to find out who that person really is.

00:11:17.388 --> 00:11:20.267
Do you know what people used to call me?

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.720
"The actress who came from a food stall".

00:11:33.344 --> 00:11:36.464
I fought for years

00:11:36.464 --> 00:11:40.603
before the industry finally accepted
that I was talented.

00:11:40.603 --> 00:11:42.560
Everyone did, except Weechana's family.

00:11:43.675 --> 00:11:45.980
I've been through hell because of them.

00:11:46.918 --> 00:11:48.720
It sucks so bad.

00:11:55.974 --> 00:11:57.775
The script on page 11.

00:12:00.203 --> 00:12:06.440
"You don't have to destroy yourself
to prove anything".

00:12:09.064 --> 00:12:15.040
From now on, do what you want to do,
for yourself.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.608
Stop worrying about whether
it'll be good enough for anyone else.

00:12:18.608 --> 00:12:21.654
The fans who truly love you

00:12:21.654 --> 00:12:24.030
will love you for who you are.

00:12:27.318 --> 00:12:30.568
And I'll be here to help you
through all of it.

00:12:30.568 --> 00:12:33.400
And I mean "all of it".

00:12:34.484 --> 00:12:37.353
Whatever you're dreaming of,

00:12:38.795 --> 00:12:40.800
I'll be right there for you.

00:12:45.014 --> 00:12:46.815
Do you get what I'm saying?

00:12:54.961 --> 00:12:57.369
I'm right here for you.

00:13:09.577 --> 00:13:11.784
Let's go.

00:13:11.784 --> 00:13:13.202
Go.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.328
Hello. I'm the head of the news department.

00:13:25.328 --> 00:13:27.129
I'm Thanwa's supervisor.

00:13:27.819 --> 00:13:29.419
Hello.

00:13:29.419 --> 00:13:30.735
Please follow me.

00:13:31.782 --> 00:13:34.320
Before it all happened,

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:37.755
he got some documents
that seemed pretty important.

00:13:37.755 --> 00:13:40.912
He said it was something big,
and then he rushed out.

00:13:40.912 --> 00:13:45.600
That means those documents
could be damaging to someone.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.510
If there's anything else you know
that might be helpful,

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.680
I'd appreciate it if you could let me know.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.408
I've been reporting against him
for a long time.

00:13:54.408 --> 00:13:58.731
If I come across anything, I'll run with it.

00:13:58.731 --> 00:14:00.216
Thank you.

00:14:01.136 --> 00:14:02.567
I'll see you later.

00:14:14.587 --> 00:14:18.614
I'll do whatever I can to help you, Eva.

00:14:18.614 --> 00:14:20.571
I'll have to tell Boat about this as well.

00:14:20.571 --> 00:14:23.040
I want us all to be on the same page.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.241
- I'll fill you in later.
- Okay.

00:14:26.624 --> 00:14:29.184
I'd really like you both

00:14:29.184 --> 00:14:32.619
to focus on helping Eva
prepare for her role first.

00:14:33.456 --> 00:14:34.715
After the election,

00:14:34.715 --> 00:14:36.936
we should be able to work things out
with Weechana's family.

00:14:36.936 --> 00:14:38.691
Got it.

00:14:38.691 --> 00:14:42.675
In that case,
I'd like to know your schedule in detail.

00:14:42.675 --> 00:14:44.483
We don't have to meet in person.

00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:47.080
We can stay in touch online
whenever it's convenient for you.

00:14:47.902 --> 00:14:49.760
You always keep your script with you, right?

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:55.336
If you ever have a couple of hours to spare,
just let me know.

00:14:55.336 --> 00:14:58.327
It doesn't matter where you are,
I'll come to you.

00:14:59.686 --> 00:15:01.038
Sure.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.000
[Weechana's Assistant]

00:15:07.526 --> 00:15:08.958
Look!

00:15:16.064 --> 00:15:17.523
Hello?

00:15:17.523 --> 00:15:20.580
Domino, are these AirPods yours?

00:15:21.701 --> 00:15:25.347
This is Eva. She went to the bathroom.

00:15:25.347 --> 00:15:26.840
AirPods?

00:15:28.075 --> 00:15:31.531
She said she couldn't find them.

00:15:31.531 --> 00:15:34.880
They were found outside Mr. Weechana's office
on the night of the party.

00:15:37.758 --> 00:15:40.926
Could you just bring it back to the gym?

00:15:40.926 --> 00:15:43.651
I'm sure you already know where it is.

00:15:43.651 --> 00:15:45.083
Thank you.

00:15:46.803 --> 00:15:48.680
Is everything okay?

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.640
Someone will drop something off for Domino.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:56.352
I need to stay with her.
It might take a while.

00:15:58.598 --> 00:16:00.784
Should we go over the script?

00:16:00.784 --> 00:16:02.091
Sure.

00:16:02.091 --> 00:16:03.238
You can go if you want.

00:16:03.238 --> 00:16:05.883
It's fine. I can stay.

00:16:05.883 --> 00:16:07.067
I've got way too much free time.

00:16:07.067 --> 00:16:09.600
Domino won't let me train someone else
during this time.

00:16:11.872 --> 00:16:13.318
It's okay.

00:16:13.318 --> 00:16:15.240
We're here with you.

00:16:21.174 --> 00:16:23.302
There's only one way.

00:16:23.302 --> 00:16:26.601
We need to leak something big
to bury that reporter story.

00:16:27.912 --> 00:16:28.979
You're right.

00:16:28.979 --> 00:16:32.720
We need to get people talking
about a scandal unrelated to the election.

00:16:35.096 --> 00:16:38.440
Then leak the story about Weechai and Pie.

00:16:40.547 --> 00:16:42.110
Grandma?

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:47.000
Someone must've caught Pie's meltdown
on video that day.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.346
We need to find the footage
and leak it immediately.

00:16:49.346 --> 00:16:51.270
If we really can't find it,

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.014
we'll just use the footage
from our security cameras.

00:16:53.014 --> 00:16:54.219
Get it done this afternoon.

00:16:54.219 --> 00:16:56.400
- Grandma?
- Yes, ma'am.

00:16:57.259 --> 00:16:58.422
Grandma, please.

00:16:58.422 --> 00:17:01.240
Don't drag Pie into the mess.

00:17:01.958 --> 00:17:06.059
Now's not the time to feel sorry for anyone.

00:17:07.264 --> 00:17:11.806
I still think Pie should help us campaign.

00:17:13.912 --> 00:17:18.040
But if we don't bury this story,
it'll be hard to campaign.

00:17:23.102 --> 00:17:25.006
Can I at least talk to her first?

00:17:25.006 --> 00:17:27.059
No, no, no.

00:17:29.392 --> 00:17:31.552
Pie can't know about this.

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:33.910
She's a woman.

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.838
She'll end up telling someone.

00:17:36.838 --> 00:17:38.354
I agree.

00:17:39.675 --> 00:17:44.195
So you want me to break up with Pie

00:17:44.195 --> 00:17:47.091
and let her think I cheated on her?

00:17:47.091 --> 00:17:49.198
Do I always have to be the bad guy
in this family?

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:51.677
What, you think
you're going to be the party leader?

00:17:51.677 --> 00:17:55.680
- Why don't you just fight me, asshole?
- You sure about that?

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.254
I'm good at this. You want a piece of me?

00:17:57.254 --> 00:17:59.984
This is my kind of thing. You want some?

00:17:59.984 --> 00:18:01.548
Hey!

00:18:03.179 --> 00:18:06.160
Why the hell are you two fighting?

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.579
Didn't we already decide on our roles
in this?

00:18:14.579 --> 00:18:16.435
My role?

00:18:16.435 --> 00:18:20.062
The role everyone shoved onto me
without asking me?

00:18:20.062 --> 00:18:22.130
I'm the one who's always stuck
doing Weechana's dirty work.

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.931
Why's that?

00:18:25.432 --> 00:18:29.520
If you can't live here,
then go live with your mom.

00:18:30.376 --> 00:18:33.822
Tell me, Grandma. Where is my mom?

00:18:33.822 --> 00:18:37.544
I know you're the reason my mother is gone.

00:18:37.544 --> 00:18:39.203
Tell me where my mom is.

00:18:39.203 --> 00:18:41.560
Tell me where the hell she is!

00:18:47.819 --> 00:18:53.603
Your mom's gone somewhere
you'll never be able to find her.

00:18:53.603 --> 00:18:55.534
- Mom.
- That's enough.

00:18:55.534 --> 00:18:57.335
Please, stop.

00:18:59.406 --> 00:19:03.166
I'm the one who calls the shots
in this house.

00:19:03.166 --> 00:19:04.851
Who stays.

00:19:04.851 --> 00:19:06.846
Who leaves.

00:19:06.846 --> 00:19:08.710
Who lives.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.511
Who dies.

00:19:11.696 --> 00:19:15.200
I make the decisions.

00:19:16.411 --> 00:19:18.212
Not you.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:54.400
You need to tell Pie
that we had no choice but to leak that story.

00:19:55.363 --> 00:19:58.960
As for her parents,
I'll deal with them myself.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:01.657
Dad...

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:06.320
Where is my mom?

00:20:09.254 --> 00:20:11.055
Dad.

00:20:13.328 --> 00:20:15.600
Where is Mom?

00:20:18.758 --> 00:20:23.720
What did Grandma mean
when she said that, Dad?

00:20:31.942 --> 00:20:33.333
Weechai.

00:20:35.286 --> 00:20:37.702
Everything we have today came at a price.

00:20:37.702 --> 00:20:40.080
Do you understand?

00:20:44.228 --> 00:20:46.920
Tell me the truth.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.443
Where is Mom?

00:20:48.443 --> 00:20:50.697
Dad, where is my mom?

00:21:13.142 --> 00:21:15.811
About that reporter,

00:21:15.811 --> 00:21:17.963
you need to clean up the mess.

00:21:17.963 --> 00:21:20.726
Make sure nothing else gets out.

00:21:20.726 --> 00:21:24.205
Keep it quiet, and do it quickly.

00:21:25.728 --> 00:21:27.142
Got it.

00:21:38.573 --> 00:21:40.747
What's the latest on Domino's AirPods?

00:21:40.747 --> 00:21:43.104
I'm about to have someone
return them to the gym, sir.

00:21:43.104 --> 00:21:46.528
Ms. Eva answered the call this morning
and told us to do it.

00:21:46.528 --> 00:21:48.329
I'll go there myself.

00:21:55.808 --> 00:21:57.771
It's the last scene. You've got this!

00:21:57.771 --> 00:21:59.980
Fighting! Come on, let's go!

00:22:00.721 --> 00:22:02.174
Okay.

00:22:02.174 --> 00:22:06.531
Institutionalization changed Muay Thai
forever,

00:22:06.531 --> 00:22:11.008
from a battlefield martial art
to a sanctioned sport.

00:22:11.008 --> 00:22:17.948
But still, every punch still carries
the history of the warrior.

00:22:18.596 --> 00:22:25.171
Institutionalization changed Muay Thai
forever,

00:22:25.171 --> 00:22:31.920
from a battlefield martial art
to a sanctioned sport.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:39.169
But still, every punch still carries
the history of the warrior.

00:22:43.136 --> 00:22:45.568
That is...

00:22:45.568 --> 00:22:47.369
so cringe.

00:22:48.166 --> 00:22:50.299
It's hard.

00:22:50.299 --> 00:22:52.320
It's very hard.

00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:55.411
Some of the words may be unfamiliar,
but if you pay close attention,

00:22:55.411 --> 00:22:58.110
you'll still recognize some familiar words
in every sentence.

00:22:58.110 --> 00:22:59.556
Do you want to try?

00:23:01.686 --> 00:23:05.360
Let's start with... the hard one.

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:07.537
Institutionalization.

00:23:07.537 --> 00:23:09.028
What?

00:23:09.028 --> 00:23:10.400
Let's try.

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:17.259
In... stil... tuti...

00:23:17.259 --> 00:23:18.523
What's that?

00:23:18.523 --> 00:23:20.230
Not bad.

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:22.240
Watch my mouth.

00:23:22.240 --> 00:23:23.795
In..

00:23:23.795 --> 00:23:25.758
- In...
- Stuh...

00:23:25.758 --> 00:23:26.862
Stuh...

00:23:26.862 --> 00:23:28.734
- Too...
- Too...

00:23:28.734 --> 00:23:29.907
Shun...

00:23:29.907 --> 00:23:32.200
- Shun...
- Nuh...

00:23:33.155 --> 00:23:35.099
- Luh...
- Luh...

00:23:35.099 --> 00:23:36.507
Zay...

00:23:36.507 --> 00:23:38.379
- Zay...
- Shun...

00:23:38.379 --> 00:23:40.011
Shun...

00:23:40.011 --> 00:23:43.760
You ready? Three... two... one.

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:47.267
- Institutionalization.
- Institutionalization.

00:23:47.267 --> 00:23:48.720
Hey, you know what? That's pretty good.

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:50.152
That's okay. That's okay.

00:23:50.152 --> 00:23:52.494
You're doing great. Don't worry.

00:23:52.494 --> 00:23:55.355
Actually... I'm serious.

00:23:55.355 --> 00:23:57.419
Your tongue just needs a little time
to get used to it.

00:23:57.419 --> 00:24:02.208
Most Thai speakers aren't used to
saying words this long.

00:24:02.208 --> 00:24:05.771
We're more familiar
with two- or three-syllable words,

00:24:05.771 --> 00:24:08.699
so placing the emphasis comes naturally.

00:24:08.699 --> 00:24:11.371
But with longer words like these,

00:24:11.371 --> 00:24:12.640
I totally understand.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:15.720
Sometimes it's hard to know
which syllable to emphasize.

00:24:16.528 --> 00:24:18.729
You're totally right.

00:24:21.984 --> 00:24:23.785
You know what?

00:24:24.608 --> 00:24:26.640
Let's drop this.

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:28.528
Let's play a game.

00:24:28.528 --> 00:24:29.761
What?

00:24:30.779 --> 00:24:33.531
- Boat, come here.
- Huh?

00:24:33.531 --> 00:24:35.870
Domino, this way, please.

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:37.671
What? Yeah?

00:24:42.259 --> 00:24:44.014
Is everything okay?

00:24:44.014 --> 00:24:46.040
Let's play a game.

00:24:54.934 --> 00:24:56.735
You want some?

00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:02.880
Okay, I will say one word in English,
with its meaning.

00:25:02.880 --> 00:25:03.359
Okay.

00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:07.101
Your task is to think of another word
that's related to it.

00:25:07.101 --> 00:25:09.494
Just say whatever comes to mind.

00:25:09.494 --> 00:25:11.696
- Ready?
- It's not that hard.

00:25:11.696 --> 00:25:13.803
- Ready to go? Let's do this.
- Ready.

00:25:13.803 --> 00:25:15.707
Let's start with...

00:25:15.707 --> 00:25:17.880
"Consequence".

00:25:18.790 --> 00:25:20.360
Result.

00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:22.560
- Result... result...
- Anybody?

00:25:22.560 --> 00:25:24.024
Anybody?

00:25:24.763 --> 00:25:27.086
- Eva.
- Hard work.

00:25:27.086 --> 00:25:28.510
Good job!

00:25:28.510 --> 00:25:30.115
One point for Eva.

00:25:30.115 --> 00:25:34.000
- Really good.
- That's quite good.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.440
Okay, next word.

00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:37.400
Let's go with...

00:25:38.238 --> 00:25:39.260
"Wacky".

00:25:39.260 --> 00:25:41.118
- Wacky?
- Wacky.

00:25:41.118 --> 00:25:43.299
Quirky or silly.

00:25:43.299 --> 00:25:44.451
- What?
- It's Boat.

00:25:44.451 --> 00:25:47.403
Oh, come on! I'm not a wacky person.

00:25:47.403 --> 00:25:48.835
- You're not?
- I am not!

00:25:48.835 --> 00:25:50.814
I am the most normal person in this room.

00:25:50.814 --> 00:25:52.854
I'm the definition of normal.

00:25:52.854 --> 00:25:54.104
- Are you sure?
- I am sure.

00:25:54.104 --> 00:25:56.760
- I'm as normal as they come.
- I don't think so.

00:25:56.760 --> 00:26:00.200
- Normal?
- Normally, I am not like this.

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:02.440
- I think that's a point for Domino.
- No!

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:05.235
No, man.

00:26:05.235 --> 00:26:07.760
Good job, good job.

00:26:07.760 --> 00:26:11.924
Next word, let's do "Safe haven".

00:26:11.924 --> 00:26:12.906
Safe haven.

00:26:12.907 --> 00:26:17.510
A place where you feel safe,
both physically and mentally, whatever.

00:26:17.510 --> 00:26:19.311
Anybody? Anybody?

00:26:21.184 --> 00:26:23.345
- Eva!
- It's you!

00:26:27.656 --> 00:26:29.680
Wait... what?

00:26:32.824 --> 00:26:36.102
You and you.

00:26:36.102 --> 00:26:39.019
You all are my safe haven.

00:26:39.019 --> 00:26:41.369
- That's right.
- Sure, I'll take that.

00:26:41.369 --> 00:26:43.227
Another point for Eva. Two points now.

00:26:43.227 --> 00:26:44.560
- Two points for me.
- Two points.

00:26:44.560 --> 00:26:45.790
Thank you.

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:48.120
Let's try a few more challenging words.

00:26:48.120 --> 00:26:49.720
Okay.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:53.214
Next, let's go with "Deadly".

00:26:53.214 --> 00:26:53.975
Daddy?

00:26:53.975 --> 00:26:55.606
- Father?
- Sugar daddy?

00:26:55.606 --> 00:26:57.387
No! No! No!

00:26:57.387 --> 00:26:59.320
Deadly.

00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:02.120
Lethal or life-threatening.

00:27:03.942 --> 00:27:05.184
Anybody?

00:27:05.184 --> 00:27:07.000
That would be me.

00:27:16.080 --> 00:27:22.360
I would consider myself very deadly...
if I wanted to.

00:27:23.966 --> 00:27:26.240
So, who wants to go first?

00:27:34.007 --> 00:27:35.921
Who wants to go first?

00:27:46.054 --> 00:27:49.440
Hey, relax. I was just kidding.

00:27:52.443 --> 00:27:54.840
Did you all understand...

00:27:56.427 --> 00:27:58.320
what I just said?

00:27:59.979 --> 00:28:02.310
Looks like you all got it.

00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:04.520
Everyone's got such serious faces.

00:28:05.467 --> 00:28:10.120
Come on, I'm not going to bite.

00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:20.000
Your teaching method is quite intriguing.

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:23.160
It's very interesting.

00:28:24.231 --> 00:28:27.441
Eva mentioned
that she's been feeling stressed lately.

00:28:30.895 --> 00:28:32.925
Honey, what brings you here?

00:28:32.925 --> 00:28:35.850
I'm in the middle of my English lesson.

00:28:54.324 --> 00:28:55.952
Thank you.

00:28:55.952 --> 00:28:58.800
I didn't expect you
to bring it over yourself.

00:29:03.611 --> 00:29:05.968
But I wanted to see you too, Eva.

00:29:05.968 --> 00:29:10.240
I've been really busy lately,
and we hardly get to talk anymore.

00:29:11.035 --> 00:29:14.810
Why don't we go grab something good to eat?

00:29:14.810 --> 00:29:16.380
Weechana!

00:29:16.380 --> 00:29:17.886
Eva!

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:22.696
Hey, Weechana.

00:29:22.696 --> 00:29:26.248
You'll be seeing Eva tomorrow
for the campaign anyway.

00:29:26.248 --> 00:29:29.811
Why don't we let Eva get some rest tonight?

00:29:29.811 --> 00:29:33.198
If there's anything to brief us on,
just send me the details.

00:29:33.198 --> 00:29:36.016
I want to go out to dinner
with my girlfriend.

00:29:36.016 --> 00:29:37.814
Her fasting window's about to start.

00:29:37.814 --> 00:29:39.640
She won't be able to eat anything.

00:29:41.382 --> 00:29:43.158
Come on.

00:29:43.158 --> 00:29:45.899
It'd be miserable to go out to eat
and not be able to eat anything.

00:29:45.899 --> 00:29:50.160
You'll get to spend the whole day with me
tomorrow anyway.

00:29:52.890 --> 00:29:56.314
I want to spend the whole night
with you, Eva.

00:29:57.878 --> 00:30:00.150
Weechana!

00:30:00.150 --> 00:30:01.658
Get in the car!

00:30:05.505 --> 00:30:07.280
You useless bastard!

00:30:07.280 --> 00:30:09.290
You have to campaign tomorrow, sir.

00:30:09.290 --> 00:30:10.822
What's the matter?

00:30:14.094 --> 00:30:16.365
Stop recording! Give it to me!

00:30:19.944 --> 00:30:21.987
Are you trying to blackmail me,
you piece of shit?

00:30:21.987 --> 00:30:23.006
Is that what you want?

00:30:23.006 --> 00:30:26.160
- Sir!
- What is it?

00:30:28.686 --> 00:30:30.487
Damn it!

00:30:39.510 --> 00:30:42.086
Delete the security camera footage.

00:30:42.086 --> 00:30:43.887
And take care of this.

00:30:52.774 --> 00:30:54.720
I'll pick you up tomorrow.

00:30:56.451 --> 00:30:59.380
When this election is over,
you'd better watch your back.

00:30:59.380 --> 00:31:01.320
Especially you.

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:17.455
Hey.

00:32:07.299 --> 00:32:08.728
Hey.

00:32:11.226 --> 00:32:14.098
I'm sorry.

00:32:15.995 --> 00:32:18.040
Why are you apologizing to me?

00:32:19.590 --> 00:32:23.840
You are all in trouble because of me.

00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:27.758
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:32:27.758 --> 00:32:30.979
Can you stop doing this?

00:32:30.979 --> 00:32:33.480
I'm the one who got everyone into this.

00:32:33.480 --> 00:32:36.400
I got you into this too.

00:32:36.400 --> 00:32:40.603
It's not your fault.
It's all that asshole's fault.

00:32:40.603 --> 00:32:44.704
Don't blame yourself.
It is not your fault at all.

00:32:44.704 --> 00:32:47.110
Don't blame yourself, either.

00:32:51.859 --> 00:32:54.051
I'm so sorry.

00:32:54.051 --> 00:32:56.720
You need to stop apologizing.

00:33:04.624 --> 00:33:07.800
Eva and Domino,

00:33:08.771 --> 00:33:11.440
we're staying right here with you.

00:33:12.328 --> 00:33:13.878
That's right.

00:33:13.878 --> 00:33:16.385
There are two of us, and two of you.

00:33:16.385 --> 00:33:18.320
So that makes four of us.

00:33:19.115 --> 00:33:22.152
Damn it, I'm not good at comforting people.

00:33:24.611 --> 00:33:26.412
Thank you.

00:33:27.606 --> 00:33:29.640
What are we going to do now?

00:33:38.886 --> 00:33:41.250
Hey, Eva.

00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:43.718
I think we need to report this to the police.

00:33:43.718 --> 00:33:46.360
No. It'll only get everyone in trouble.

00:33:47.851 --> 00:33:50.320
Is there anything else we should know?

00:33:52.804 --> 00:33:54.761
You're better off not knowing.

00:33:55.470 --> 00:33:58.334
I'll do my best in this election.

00:33:58.334 --> 00:34:00.136
I made a deal with his grandma.

00:34:00.136 --> 00:34:03.400
She said she'd let me go
once the election is over.

00:34:04.136 --> 00:34:08.400
The only person who can stop Weechana
is his grandma.

00:34:09.419 --> 00:34:12.542
That is, if she keeps her word.

00:34:12.542 --> 00:34:16.219
She will. She hates me more than anything.

00:34:16.219 --> 00:34:18.368
I believe she'll let you go.

00:34:18.368 --> 00:34:19.899
But with that family,

00:34:19.899 --> 00:34:24.230
who knows if their idea of "letting you go"
is the same as ours?

00:34:28.091 --> 00:34:31.797
What about the video?
Did you keep it where I told you to?

00:34:31.797 --> 00:34:33.632
Wait, wait.

00:34:33.632 --> 00:34:35.744
What are you two talking about?

00:34:35.744 --> 00:34:37.462
I'm confused.

00:34:37.462 --> 00:34:39.024
This is way more serious than I thought.

00:34:39.024 --> 00:34:41.980
I think you should tell us.

00:34:44.424 --> 00:34:46.824
I'll tell you another time.

00:34:46.824 --> 00:34:48.499
I'm just really tired today.

00:34:48.499 --> 00:34:52.093
I'm sorry for getting the two of you
involved in all this.

00:34:52.093 --> 00:34:55.760
I'll do my best to keep everyone safe.

00:35:01.054 --> 00:35:03.130
You're forgetting about yourself again.

00:35:07.384 --> 00:35:09.200
I will be fine.

00:35:10.870 --> 00:35:12.980
Thanks for keeping us company.

00:35:15.854 --> 00:35:17.720
And thanks for taking us home.

00:35:18.398 --> 00:35:20.199
Let's go.

00:35:32.024 --> 00:35:33.784
Do you think they can handle this?

00:35:33.784 --> 00:35:37.785
What about us?
Do you think we can handle this?

00:35:37.785 --> 00:35:40.006
We can't leave them behind.

00:35:40.006 --> 00:35:43.392
It's just the two of them.
And they're both women.

00:35:44.224 --> 00:35:47.126
I wasn't going to leave them behind.

00:35:47.126 --> 00:35:50.251
There are only two of us, remember?

00:35:50.251 --> 00:35:53.995
We only got through today
because there were just two guards.

00:35:53.995 --> 00:35:56.571
Next time,
we don't know how many they'll send,

00:35:56.571 --> 00:35:58.502
or what they'll do to us.

00:35:58.502 --> 00:36:00.512
We'll just do everything we can.

00:36:00.512 --> 00:36:02.330
The campaign will be over soon,

00:36:02.330 --> 00:36:04.520
and then we'll see what happens.

00:36:05.169 --> 00:36:07.944
Okay, fine.

00:36:07.944 --> 00:36:09.480
Should we go?

00:36:09.480 --> 00:36:13.960
They've been up there for quite a while.
I think they're okay.

00:36:13.960 --> 00:36:17.606
We kicked some serious ass today.

00:36:17.606 --> 00:36:20.763
But if I'm gonna die,
I don't want it to be from dengue.

00:36:20.763 --> 00:36:22.230
That's just a dumb way to die.

00:36:22.230 --> 00:36:24.580
There are so many damn mosquitoes.

00:36:28.533 --> 00:36:30.688
Sure, let's go.

00:36:30.688 --> 00:36:33.408
Thank you, sir.

00:36:33.408 --> 00:36:34.787
Let's go.

00:37:01.915 --> 00:37:03.842
- Are you finished?
- Yes.

00:37:03.842 --> 00:37:06.043
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

00:37:18.675 --> 00:37:21.699
- Domino?
- Yeah?

00:37:21.699 --> 00:37:24.024
Could you follow us in your car?

00:37:24.749 --> 00:37:29.320
I'd like a little time alone
with my girlfriend.

00:37:31.400 --> 00:37:33.480
Even just a few minutes would be nice.

00:37:35.411 --> 00:37:37.520
I'm asking nicely here.

00:37:39.533 --> 00:37:40.771
Okay.

00:37:40.771 --> 00:37:42.930
Alright. Let me go get my car keys.

00:37:42.930 --> 00:37:44.435
I'll follow you.

00:37:44.435 --> 00:37:47.118
Sure, I'll wait here.

00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:41.864
Are you ready?

00:38:41.864 --> 00:38:44.480
Wait, we need to wait for Domino.

00:38:45.112 --> 00:38:47.288
Eva, we're running late.

00:38:47.288 --> 00:38:49.229
Everyone's already there.

00:38:49.229 --> 00:38:51.910
Besides, she already has the location, right?

00:38:51.910 --> 00:38:54.944
Can't you wait just a little longer?
She will be down in a minute.

00:38:54.944 --> 00:38:58.160
And she will follow us in a minute.

00:39:00.411 --> 00:39:02.370
Okay?

00:39:02.370 --> 00:39:04.171
Let's go.